         [0092]    One of skill in the art will appreciate that a variety of methods are evident from the above-provided description and included within the scope of the present invention as disclosed. Thus, according to one method of the invention, a first hole is drilled or pierced into a substrate such as a bone. A cannulated insertion tool  2300 , as shown in  FIG. 23  has a suture  2302  disposed generally longitudinally adjacent to a first substantially solid shaft  2304  thereof. The first shaft  2304  is used to drive a self-tapping stopper portion  2306  into the hole by a leftward rotation of the first shaft  2304 . Subsequently, a further portion of the cannulated insertion tool, including a second cannulated shaft  2308  coaxially encircling the first substantially solid shaft  2304  is used to drive a self-tapping fixing portion  2310  into the hole by a rightward rotation of the second shaft  2308  until the stopper portion  2306  and the fixing portion  2310  engage and lock together. Thereafter the opposing sense of the threads  2312 ,  2314  of the stopper portion and of the fixing portion respectively prevent subsequent rotation and withdrawal of the resulting anchor assembly  2320 . 
