     However, if any one of the points (n-1,Pp(n-1)), (n,Pp(n)), and (n+1,Pp(n+1)) is above a line connecting the points (n+2,Pp(n+2)) and (n-2,Pp(n-2)), since it means that the envelope line is within the range of the average blood pressure away from the area corresponding to the maximum blood pressure, a(n) is set as zero. 
